															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thegreatgimmick" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2890370); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2890370&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606467195" alt="TheGreatGimmick" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2890370)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thegreatgimmick" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2890370); return false;" >TheGreatGimmick</a></span> <span class="odate time_1480766730 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">03 Dec 2016 12:05</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2702728">
									

<p>This is my first attempt at an SCP object. Although the basic idea is quite simple, I think it still has the potential to create some interesting situations and interactions.</p>
<p>My style of writing is not exactly 'character-driven', so most of this is clinical descriptions of mechanics and events; I'd like to think this is in the spirit of the original SCPs, although some might find it boring in comparison to some of the more 'story-like' entries of late. I hope it is still interesting to enough people to allow my first attempt to be a success.</p>
<p>Thank you for your time and feedback!</p>

							</div>

								
					
