				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/khaim" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1796098); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1796098&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606467195" alt="Khaim" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1796098)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/khaim" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1796098); return false;" >Khaim</a></span> <span class="odate time_1480803243 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">03 Dec 2016 22:14</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2702983">
									

<p>It's ambitious, that's for sure. For a first try I think it's quite good. The general idea has been done before, but that's fine - you can always try to write a better version.</p>
<p>Style is mostly good. The language around &quot;events&quot; is stilted, and you repeat some things between the SCP and description. Same with the logs: you give away several facts in the description that make the corresponding log less interesting because the reader already knows what they find. And some logs are just dull: E-8 could be replaced with &quot;the bulb reforms after each event&quot; in the description.</p>
<p>I also feel like there's too much detail given. The foundation knows almost exactly how this thing works. It may be weird, but it's completely understood. I'd like it better if they didn't have an equation predicting precisely when it's going to jump.</p>
<p>Overall I like it, but I recommend deleting words. Lots of words.</p>

							</div>

								
					
