				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sound-chaser" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1664092); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1664092&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606467196" alt="Sound Chaser" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1664092)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sound-chaser" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1664092); return false;" >Sound Chaser</a></span> <span class="odate time_1480784439 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">03 Dec 2016 17:00</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2702868">
									

<p>This shows an admirable amount of effort having been put into a very simple object, and it's a brave attempt, it just doesn't quite work for me. On the plus side, I do like that you've been thorough in exploring every avenue this thing presents, and I really like Addendum B in this regard. The sterilisation idea is particularly interesting, although I'm not so fond of the rejected neutralisation, which is largely pointless.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;I'm&nbsp;having&nbsp;some&nbsp;issues&nbsp;with&nbsp;it,&nbsp;though</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;And&nbsp;here&nbsp;they&nbsp;are</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The main problem here is that it's&#8230; it's just too <em>long</em>. By the last collapsible, it really feels dragged out; nothing there is particularly notable except the rock-egg things from Event 2609-180, and that's immediately brushed under the rug. Most of the last collapsible, in fact, isn't majorly interesting in my eyes and could be cut without really harming the rest of the article.</p>
<p>The crosslinking has mixed success for me; the first one makes sense as an experiment, but the 523 mention is totally pointless except just for something to happen, and that something is mostly relevant to 523 anyway. I suppose, in my eyes, the fact that it's the last thing there makes it worse. This article is long enough to make at least me want some sort of payoff in the end, and the fact that that's all we get just leaves me with a sense of &quot;Oh&#8230; all right then.&quot;</p>
<p>A problem I have with the actual writing is the repetition and lack of concision. Many of the sentences here feel like, if edited a bit, they could result in the page being half as long. For instance:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This can cause teleported matter to ‘overlap’ with matter already present at the new location. The teleported overlapping matter appears to take priority over matter already present at the new location, causing the already present matter to disappear where there is overlap with the teleported matter.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>could easily be shortened to:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This can cause teleported matter to ‘overlap’ with matter already present at the new location, causing the former to completely replace the latter</p>
</blockquote>
<p>or something like that. Admittedly, mine's just an example, but something along those lines would be a lot less tiring to read.</p>
<p>The simplicity of the central item isn't necessarily a bad thing, but to be honest, there isn't really enough done with it here to win my heart. Not that it's unsalvageable; perhaps you could just look at one of the ideas you've brought up and put that at the focus of the article.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, I'm impressed with the level of dedication that's gone into this, and with some heavy rewriting, something along these lines could work, but as it is, I'm sorry, it's just too boring for me.</p>

