<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Most&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;last&nbsp;collapsible,&nbsp;in&nbsp;fact,&nbsp;isn't&nbsp;majorly&nbsp;interesting&nbsp;in&nbsp;my&nbsp;eyes...&nbsp;</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>&#8230; and could be cut without really harming the rest of the article.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I find this fascinating, albeit in an incredulous manner. To clarify I don't mean that in a negative way, just that it is the exact opposite of what I was expecting. The 'Events' are where the concept is really fleshed out, showing a sampling of situations this &quot;blasted lamp&quot; tends to create. Can you explain in more detail why you feel it was not all that interesting?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;the&nbsp;523&nbsp;mention&nbsp;is&nbsp;totally&nbsp;pointless&nbsp;except&nbsp;just&nbsp;for&nbsp;something&nbsp;to&nbsp;happen</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;the&nbsp;523&nbsp;mention&nbsp;is&nbsp;totally&nbsp;pointless&nbsp;except&nbsp;just&nbsp;for&nbsp;something&nbsp;to&nbsp;happen&nbsp;</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I wanted an Event to occur where SCP-2609 causes an incident with another SCP. I picked SCP-523 simply because its anomalous abilities were such that things could go very badly very fast due to even a minor distraction, much less a blinding flash of life. Do you have a suggestion for an SCP that would feel more natural, or do you simply not like the concept of SCP-2609 causing an incident?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;...&nbsp;the&nbsp;fact&nbsp;that&nbsp;it's&nbsp;the&nbsp;last&nbsp;thing&nbsp;there&nbsp;makes&nbsp;it&nbsp;worse.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;&nbsp;...&nbsp;the&nbsp;fact&nbsp;that&nbsp;it's&nbsp;the&nbsp;last&nbsp;thing&nbsp;there&nbsp;makes&nbsp;it&nbsp;worse.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>This article is long enough to make at least me want some sort of payoff in the end, and the fact that that's all we get just leaves me with a sense of &quot;Oh… all right then.&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I think that this complaint has to do with this entry trying to 'go back to the roots' of SCPs, for lack of a better way to say what I mean. Although the many story-like, character-driven SCPs nowadays are still great in their own way, the clinical 'report' style and the relative absence of actual characters were what made the original SCPs unique and thus what made me like the old ones. There is no &quot;payoff&quot; in this entry because this is not a story, it is a document.</p>
<p>Do you think this is just a difference of opinion, or something I can work on to fix? If you think I can fix it, how?</p>
<p>How much do you think it would help if I simply swapped the order of the experiment and event logs? Then it is not at the end, and moreover the 'Pending Experiments' thing (which you liked) is actually a natural ending for the article, giving hints about what might happen in the future.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;A&nbsp;problem&nbsp;I&nbsp;have&nbsp;with&nbsp;the&nbsp;actual&nbsp;writing&nbsp;is&nbsp;the&nbsp;repetition&nbsp;and&nbsp;lack&nbsp;of&nbsp;concision.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;&nbsp;A&nbsp;problem&nbsp;I&nbsp;have&nbsp;with&nbsp;the&nbsp;actual&nbsp;writing&nbsp;is&nbsp;the&nbsp;repetition&nbsp;and&nbsp;lack&nbsp;of&nbsp;concision.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>You're not the first to say this, and its definitely something I need to work on. Thank you!</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;perhaps&nbsp;...&nbsp;look&nbsp;at&nbsp;one&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;ideas&nbsp;you've&nbsp;brought&nbsp;up&nbsp;and&nbsp;put&nbsp;that&nbsp;at&nbsp;the&nbsp;focus&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;article.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;&nbsp;perhaps&nbsp;you&nbsp;could&nbsp;just&nbsp;look&nbsp;at&nbsp;one&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;ideas&nbsp;you've&nbsp;brought&nbsp;up&nbsp;and&nbsp;put&nbsp;that&nbsp;at&nbsp;the&nbsp;focus&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;article.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>What 'ideas' do you refer to here?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Thank you for your time and feedback!</p>

