<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;3</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>523's the main star</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That's what I found to be amusing in a deadpan-like way. Despite all of its vast potential and un-containability, SCP-2609 is, at the end of the day, a lamp. It does not <em>mean</em> to escape the most secure locations on the planet every few weeks, it did not <em>mean</em> to drop those people off that cliff, it does not have any intentions of using its apparently unlimited spacial powers for any grand design, because it has no intentions at all; its a lamp. It won't attack, it won't infiltrate, it won't make people go crazy; it just does its thing.</p>
<p>So, I just liked how it just shows up and does nothing else, because, well, its a lamp. I find the whole situation to be slightly amusing (SCP-523 basically just like 'well this works out great for me' while SCP-2609 just sits there and flickers). This could just be a difference of opinion again, but if you disagree, please, discuss it further!</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
