<p>This is REALLY late, but I've just now seen it, so I might as well respond 8 months later than never haha</p>
<p>I don't know how 'secrets' work on this site, so, potential &quot;spoilers&quot;:</p>
<p>The 'hidden' idea was that the Lamp only takes living things that can experience its light. Bacteria can actually sense light levels, as can flies, as can crippled/whole people. But a heart can't, nor can one who is brain dead. What is not explicitly mentioned in the experiment is that</p>
<ul>
<li>the brain dead body and the heart were both devoid of the bacteria that were within them following the event</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>experimentation on viruses / prions yielded the expected results for the wrong reasons: the Foundation thinks it is because viruses / prions are not alive, while the real reason is that they cannot experience light.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>experimentation was not thought to be done on blind individuals, but if the Foundation were to do so, they would discover that blind living things are not teleported.</li>
</ul>

